{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-6580",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/0204cfb247273efc20a31366dcb84096d630aa6dbe90c94a8802834205bbdd56.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$",
